## Why This Is Asked

Assesses practical CISSP concepts for edge-to-cloud security in a high-velocity fleet context, including hardware-backed identity, secure update, provenance, and incident response.

## Key Concepts

- Edge attestation with TPM/TEE
- Ephemeral credentials and mTLS
- SBOM and reproducible builds (Sigstore/SLSA)
- Runtime integrity and OTA security
- Incident response, tabletop exercises, and tooling

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo-code: verify firmware signature on boot
function verifyFirmware(signature, payload) {
  const isValid = verifySignature(payload, signature);
  if (!isValid) throw new Error('Invalid firmware');
  bootMeetsIntegrityChecks();
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you scale attestation verification across 200k devices?
- What tooling would you use for SBOM generation and artifact signing at the edge?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests practical CISSP alignment on secure messaging design: threat modeling, cryptography, device attestation, revocation, and incident response, across multiple platforms.

## Key Concepts
- End-to-end encryption and forward secrecy
- Device attestation and binding keys to a trusted device
- Key rotation, revocation, and audit logging
- Threat modeling methods (STRIDE/PASTA)

## Code Example
```javascript
// Example: rotate per-user keys (simplified)
async function rotateUserKey(userId) {
  const newKey = await crypto.subtle.generateKey({name:'AES-GCM', length:256}, true, ['encrypt','decrypt']);
  await storeKey(userId, newKey);
  await revokeOldKeys(userId);
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you validate key compromise containment in a live system?
- What logs and metrics would you collect to support forensics without exposing plaintext data?
